"Build the slow, last-phase test suite that drives the real Rust SpacetimeDB module end-to-end in an isolated test world. Approach: run spacetime in dev via po (spacetime start / publish). Since launching spacetime is a system dependency, gate E2E behind a bun TS wrapper test that first verifies system prerequisites (required programs installed and at acceptable versions) before using them, skipping/failing clearly if unmet. Isolate each run: publish to a throwaway uniquely-named database per run (or fixed name + --delete-data); seed a minimal deterministic AssetPack via push_assets (set LocationMap rng_seed for reproducible map gen); force ticks by calling run_system explicitly (it is unguarded) rather than waiting on the 1s scheduler; assert on table state via spacetime sql (as the owner identity for non-public component tables); tear down via spacetime delete. Cover: combat pipeline (act -> shift_queued_action -> action_system damage math max(0,dmg+atk-def) -> event.resolve -> hp_system; damage resolves across >=2 ticks), map-generation determinism per seed, and push_assets idempotency. Wire as a po process test-integration and add as the final phase of the verify bundle (check -> test-web -> test-rust -> test-integration) so cheap failures short-circuit before this expensive phase. Note: reducers/systems cannot be unit-tested in-process (ReducerContext is not constructible outside a running module), so this instance-backed harness is the only way to cover them end-to-end."